# Temporal.Now (docs/temporal.md, "Host clock"): it reads the host clock,
# which `@clock <epoch nanoseconds>` sets (sjs_vm_set_clock), and nothing
# else. Every expected value was generated by temporal-polyfill 1.0.5 (the
# vendored tests/vendor/temporal-polyfill, whose Temporal.Now diff-node
# gives the same instant: its Date.now the clock's milliseconds, the
# nanoseconds past them added) and is the same in @js-temporal/polyfill
# 0.5.1 (its Now as the specification defines it from the instant: the
# Instant, at the time zone). A RangeError or a TypeError there is a fault
# here. A case named "deliberate" faults where JavaScript gives a value: a
# case with no @clock that reads the clock (JavaScript reads the machine's),
# a time zone's name or an ISO string's time zone (time zone data), and
# zonedDateTimeISO (no ZonedDateTime).

# --- Every function at clocks before and after the epoch, beside midnight,
# past an int64 of nanoseconds and at the limits

